        "original_id": "5bb6b7c1-0ecb-5d2d-8845-f909579e18a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Rescuers, The Muppets, The Fox and the Hound, Macbeth\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Buena Vista Distribution\n- People: Jeanette Nolan\n- Topics: animated films, musical comedy films, television series roles, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- Macbeth is a 1948 film in which Jeanette Nolan had a role.\n- Jeanette Nolan is best known for roles in the television series The Virginian from 1962 to 1971 and Dirty Sally in 1974.\n- The Rescuers is a 1977 American animated comedy-drama adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions and first released on June 22, 1977, by Buena Vista Distribution.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Ellie Mae in the Disney animated film The Rescuers in 1977.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Widow Tweed in the Disney animated film The Fox and the Hound in 1981.\n- The Muppets is a 2011 American musical comedy film and the seventh theatrical film featuring the Muppets.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
